---
// Acceptable Use Policy — attorney-final text (source: 01-legal-entity/drafts-for-attorney/
// Final-Docs-8-26-2026/"7 - Acceptable Use Policy - Final.docx", Allen L., 08/26/2026).
//
// NEW PAGE 08/26/2026. Previously the acceptable-use terms lived as a SECTION inside
// /terms/; the attorney's final Terms §10 restructures it into a separately posted
// document incorporated by reference, so it needs its own URL.
//
// ⚠ DO NOT DEPLOY BEFORE /terms/ IS ALSO UPDATED to the attorney-final text. The
// section numbers cited below (6, 14, 18) are the NUMBERED sections of the final
// Terms. The currently-live /terms/ page has 18 UNNUMBERED headings and no copyright
// section at all, so these cross-references dangle until that page is converted.
//
// Item 7 ("Use our output to decide something about another person") is NOT boilerplate:
// per the attorney memo (Q7), it is the CONDITION of an exclusion under Colorado
// SB 26-189, which excludes content-generating technology only where an acceptable use
// policy prohibits the generated content from being used in a consequential decision.
// Do not remove or soften it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Acceptable Use Policy — AdaptiveResume"
  description="The short list of things you agree not to do with AdaptiveResume: no fabricated credentials, no abuse of the free scan, and no using what we generate to make decisions about other people."
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A short list, and none of it should be a surprise. The product is built not to invent
        anything about you — most of what follows is just asking you not to fight that.
      </p>
      <p class="effective">Effective date: 09/01/2026</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This Acceptable Use Policy is part of our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>. When you
          use AdaptiveResume, you agree not to do any of the following.
        </p>

        <ol class="rules">
          <li>
            <strong>Break the law.</strong> Do not use the Service for any unlawful purpose or in
            violation of any applicable law or regulation.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Commit fraud with it.</strong> Do not attempt to make the Service fabricate
            credentials, licenses, degrees, or work history. Do not use it to build a resume for a
            false or stolen identity, and do not use its output in furtherance of employment,
            immigration, or benefits fraud. The product is designed not to invent anything; trying
            to defeat that design is a violation, not a workaround.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Abuse the free and make-it-right surfaces.</strong> Do not automate or bulk-run
            the free scan or the demo, and do not use the make-it-right process to obtain the paid
            review and then request a refund outside the conditions set out in Section 6 of the
            <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Attack or drain the Service.</strong> Do not probe, scan, or test its
            vulnerabilities except with our written permission, evade rate limits, scrape it, resell
            access to it, or build a competing dataset or model from its output.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Upload what is not yours to give.</strong> Do not upload files you have no right
            to provide, including someone else's resume without their authority, and do not upload
            malware or content designed to disrupt processing. Use of the Service by or on behalf of
            an organization is governed by a separate written commercial agreement, not by these
            consumer terms.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Misrepresent us.</strong> Do not imply that AdaptiveResume verified, endorsed,
            or guaranteed your credentials or your outcomes to any employer or to anyone else.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Use our output to decide something about another person.</strong> Content
            generated by the Service is for the use of the person whose career history it describes.
            Do not use it, and do not give it to anyone else to use, as a basis for making a
            consequential decision about any individual, including any decision about employment or
            an employment opportunity, education, housing, lending or other financial services,
            insurance, health care, or government benefits. The Service does not screen, score,
            rank, or evaluate candidates, and it may not be used as though it did.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate an account for violating this policy, as described in Section
          14 of the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>. To report abuse, or to send a copyright
          notice under Section 18 of the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>, write to
          <a href="mailto:support@adaptiveresume.com">support@adaptiveresume.com</a> or to
          AdaptiveResume LLC, 8735 Dunwoody Place, Suite N, Atlanta, Georgia 30350.
        </p>
      </div>

      <nav class="legal-links" aria-label="Other legal pages">
        <span class="muted">Related:</span>
        <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .container.narrow { max-width: 70ch; }
    .effective { font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 28px; }
    .prose { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .prose h2 { margin-top: 1.8em; font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--ink); }
    .prose ul { padding-left: 1.2em; }
    .prose li { margin-bottom: .5em; }
    .prose strong { color: var(--ink); }
    .rules { padding-left: 1.2em; }
    .rules li { margin-bottom: 1.1em; }
    .legal-links { margin-top: 44px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  </style>
</Base>
